<title>GREECE: GREEK MUTUAL FUND ASSETS HIT 4.82 TRLN DRS IN Q1.</title>
<headline>GREEK MUTUAL FUND ASSETS HIT 4.82 TRLN DRS IN Q1.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek mutual fund assets under management rose 5.3 percent in March, 244 billion drachmas, to end the first quarter at 4.82 trillion, an increase of 26.3 percent since the beginning of the year.</p>
<p>Money market funds made the lion's share of total assets at 58.9 percent followed by fixed income funds with 37.1 percent.</p>
<p>Equity growth funds made up only 2.5 percent of the total with balanced funds an even lower 1.4 percent, the association of institutional investors said in its monthly review. --George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
